Line 27: "n" is a number, which has no variants to check.
    check which kind n is:
                     ^
"check which kind" tells apart the variants of a kind defined with "is one of:" (like "a shape is one of:"), or a value that can be nothing.

Line 41: I don't know anything called "inside".
    say inside.
        ^^^^^^
You made "inside" inside the "when" on line 37, so it only exists inside that block. To use it afterwards, make it before the "when".

Line 44: "stop the loop" only works inside a loop.
            stop the loop.
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It leaves the loop it's in. To end the whole program, write "stop the program".
